    "title" "Train Cargo Tools"
    "description" "[h1]Train Cargo Tools[/h1]
Trains already move shapes and fluids in dense containers. This mod lets you do the same thing off the rails.

Pack shapes or fluids into the game's own cargo containers, carry them on a cargo belt, buffer them in a cargo store, and unpack them where you need them. Train stations take the containers straight from a belt, so a station no longer has to be the only place cargo exists.

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Shape and Fluid Cargo Packagers[/b] - 360 shapes, or 60 fluid, into one container.
[*][b]Shape and Fluid Cargo Unpackagers[/b] - the container back onto a space belt or pipe.
[*][b]Cargo Belts[/b] - drag them like a space belt. Corners, junctions and lifts are placed for you.
[*][b]Cargo Stores[/b] - 75 containers, 25 on each floor, of any type at once.
[/list]

All of it lives in the [b]Train Cargo[/b] group on the hotbar, and there are wiki pages for each building in game.

[h2]Why bother[/h2]
A cargo belt runs at a fifth of a space belt's speed and uses one lane per floor instead of four. It still moves about [b]18x[/b] the shapes, because every slot carries 360 of them. For fluid the figure is about [b]3x[/b] a space pipe.

Buffering is the bigger jump: a chunk of cargo belt holds 4,320 shapes against a space belt's 192.

Cargo belts only talk to other cargo machines. They will not take input from a space belt or a space pipe, so a line cannot be fed by accident.

[h2]Junctions and lifts[/h2]
Drag a cargo belt into another one and you get a junction, which splits its containers evenly between the routes leading away from it - one in, two or three out. Drag one into something in its way and you get a lift, which ramps up or down a floor or two and carries on.

Both are placed automatically, the way the game places belt corners. Neither is in the hotbar.

[h2]Research[/h2]
Two nodes in the trains group, 4.8k points each:
[list]
[*][b]Cargo Machines[/b] - packagers, unpackagers and cargo belts.
[*][b]Cargo Stores[/b] - the store.
[/list]

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]This mod affects save games.[/b] Once you install it to a save, you cannot play that save without it.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

Bugs and requests: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Mods/issues
Licensed under Apache 2.0."
}
